---
import DetailPage from '../../layouts/DetailPage.astro';
import SceneStage from '../../components/SceneStage.astro';

const prev = { href: '/science/platform', label: 'Platform' };
---

<DetailPage
  title="Generalizability Measurements — DiligenceBio"
  description="Assess whether frontier models learned the biology you need — not whether they fit the data they were given. Explainability and generalizability metrics for intelligent systems."
  parent={{ href: '/science', label: 'Our science' }}
  index="02"
  heading="Generalizability Measurements"
  claim="Assess whether frontier models learned the biology you need."
  prev={prev}
>
  <p>A model can use biology without having learned it.</p>
  <p>
    Our science focuses on explainability and generalizability of intelligent systems, toward
    decoding biological complex systems by distillation and encoding them to AI. Our science
    similarly views AI as a complex system, and tests whether the AI actually learns biology.
  </p>
  <p>
    Accuracy on a held-out split says a model fits the data it was given. Generalizability
    metrics ask a different question: does the model carry an understanding that survives a new
    target, a new assay, a new patient population — the conditions your next decision will
    actually be made in.
  </p>

  <Fragment slot="stage">
    <SceneStage kicker="Our science — live" title="GENERALIZABILITY" prev={prev} />
  </Fragment>
</DetailPage>

<script>
  import { initSceneStage } from '../../scripts/sceneStage';
  import { frontierScene, SCIENCE_LAYOUT } from '../../scripts/science';
  import { loadSettings } from '../../scripts/settings';

  const stage = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-page-stage]');
  if (stage) {
    const panel = initSceneStage(stage, { scene: frontierScene(), ...SCIENCE_LAYOUT });
    loadSettings().then(({ science }) => {
      if (science) panel.update({ speed: science.speed, mono: science.mono });
    });
  }
</script>
